#: ../../AIDE/Specifications_PF.rst:142
msgid "LFOM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../AIDE/Specifications_PF.rst:127
msgid "The plant entrance tank is equipped with a flow-measurement device designed to produce a linear relationship between plant flow and the water level in the entrance chamber. The standard device is the Linear Flow Orifice Meter (LFOM), which has a pattern of orifices through which flow exits the entrance tank. A demonstrated equivalent, such as a Sutro weir, can be substituted in a project-specific configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../AIDE/Specifications_PF.rst:129
msgid "The orifice pattern is designed so that the water level in the entrance chamber (equal to the hydrostatic head pushing water through the orifices) is linearly proportional to the total flow through the orifices (equal to the plant flow). An example of an LFOM is shown in :numref:`figure_spec_PF_LFOM`. Depending on the configuration, the orifices are drilled in a flat plate or in the walls of a vertical pipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../AIDE/Specifications_PF.rst:131
msgid "The LFOM measures flows from at least 25 percent to 100 percent of the maximum plant design flow. Project-specific configurations can extend the measurement range to lower flow rates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../AIDE/Specifications_PF.rst:133
msgid "To provide adequate flow-measurement resolution, the water level changes by at least 20 cm from no flow to the design flow rate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../AIDE/Specifications_PF.rst:142
msgid "Example of a Linear Flow Orifice Meter."
msgstr ""

